{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"appetitive-catatonic-doe","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# `binding_store.py` is at 787/800 — extract the last-synced-peer-state cluster\n\nRaised by the operator while reviewing change 1296 (ticket 88d9): \"We're adding a lot to\nbinding_store.py. Should we split that out to preemptively avoid the 800 LOC cap?\" Measured rather\nthan estimated: the file was **749** LOC, 1296 takes it to **787**, and the cap is **800**. Thirteen\nlines of headroom, and the CI module-size gate fails the build when ANY `src/rebar` file exceeds the\ncap — so the next contributor to touch this file breaks the build, having added nothing wrong.\n\nDeliberately NOT done inside 1296: that change is a data-loss fix that needed to land promptly, and\nbundling a structural refactor into it would have made it slower to review and harder to reason about.\nThe docstrings added there were tightened instead (795 -> 787) to buy immediate headroom.\n\n## The seam, which already exists\n\n`binding_store.py` holds two distinct concerns:\n\n1. **binding lifecycle** — bind / confirm / unbind, absence + rekey handling, GC/retire grace, the\n   immutable numeric Jira id (bug 7c26). This is the bulk of the file.\n2. **last-synced PEER STATE** — the ADR-0026 three-way-merge baseline (`get_baseline`, `set_baseline`,\n   `seed_baselines_from_snapshot`, `_BASELINE_FIELDS`) plus the peer-parent evidence channel added by\n   1296 (`get_peer_parent`, `set_peer_parent`). Together ~130 LOC with docstrings — comfortably over\n   the policy's 100-LOC floor for a new module, and a genuine cohesive concern: \"what did the peer\n   look like the last time we successfully looked\".\n\nConcern 2 has its own ADR, its own absence semantics (\"an ABSENT baseline is VALID and degrades to\nlocal-wins\"), and its own advance site in the pass (`reconcile._advance_baselines` /\n`_advance_peer_parent`). Its consumers are `outbound_field_diff`, `binding_walk` and now\n`inbound_fields` — none of which touch binding lifecycle.\n\n## What makes this non-trivial, stated honestly\n\nThese are METHODS on `BindingStore`, not free functions, so this is not a file move. Extraction means\neither module-level helpers taking the entry dict (the store keeps thin delegating methods, so no\ncaller changes) or a mixin. The first is preferable — it keeps the public surface identical, so every\nexisting call site and every test double stays valid, and it makes the peer-state functions directly\nunit-testable without constructing a store.\n\nPer the module-size policy this must be split ALONG THE SEAM ABOVE and not mechanically to hit a\nnumber, and the new module must not fall under 100 LOC.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `binding_store.py` is under 700 LOC, and the new module is over 100\n- [ ] `BindingStore`'s public surface is UNCHANGED — no call site and no test double is edited to\n      accommodate the split, asserted by the fact that the reconciler suites pass untouched\n- [ ] the peer-state functions are directly unit-testable without constructing a `BindingStore`, and\n      at least one new test does so (otherwise the extraction bought nothing)\n- [ ] `_BASELINE_FIELDS` moves WITH the cluster, and `outbound_field_diff` / `binding_walk` /\n      `inbound_fields` still resolve their reads (a grep-backed consumer list recorded on this ticket)\n- [ ] the absence semantics survive the move verbatim: absent baseline degrades to local-wins, absent\n      peer parent degrades to NO CLEAR. A test pins each, because these are the properties that make\n      the cluster safe and a refactor is exactly when they get quietly dropped\n- [ ] the module-size gate passes, and the full reconciler unit + integration suites pass","id":"4522-e600-9e2c-4823","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"binding_store.py is at 787/800: extract the last-synced-peer-state cluster"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785774576590337001,"uuid":"583a45cc-0e87-43da-b4bd-8cef86449a9e"}